# Human comprehension gate (global)

Agent Dev Kit is installed globally at `~/.cursor/agent_dev_kit`. In the **Cursor IDE**, this rule applies in **every project** — no per-project kit install required. The **Cursor CLI** (`agent` binary) does not read `~/.cursor/rules/`; run `./scripts/kit install --target=cursor --project` per repo so this gate also applies there.

The developer is the **control plane**. Highly reliable automation reduces monitoring; kit counters that with an explicit human gate before commit.

## Before commit or PR (non-trivial work)

1. Write `.ai/work/{work_ref}-handoff.md` in the **current project repo** (create `.ai/work/` if missing).
2. Generate **3 comprehension questions** from the handoff — human answers in their own words.
3. Wait for explicit **human sign-off**. Do not fill sign-off or Q&A for the human.
4. Only then run verification or commit.

**Default tier:** standard. Skip only when the human explicitly says comprehension minimal (typo, comment-only).

Full rules: [COMPREHENSION.md](../agent_dev_kit/docs/guidelines/COMPREHENSION.md)

Also load via `~/.cursor/kit-user-rules.manifest.json` → `always_load_kit_guidelines_resolved`.
